{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSeveral authoritative-looking doc entry points have drifted from the current contracts (audit ae1b). Grounded, current locations:\n- **Bare `--assignee <handle>` examples** teach a Jira-UNRESOLVABLE value: `README.md:44` (`rebar claim \"$tid\" --assignee alice`), `docs/user-guide.md:115` (`rebar claim <ticket-id> --assignee alice`), `docs/user-guide.md:229` (`--assignee=bob`). Yet `docs/config.md:431` states the assignee must be a **Jira-resolvable identity (email or accountId)** — a bare handle is silently cleared by the next reconcile.\n- **MCP navigation mis-route**: `docs/README.md:25` routes \"Drive rebar over MCP\" → `llm-framework.md`, not the generated `docs/mcp-reference.md` (the complete tool reference, named at `docs/README.md:77`).\n- **Removed config surface**: `docs/README.md:91` still describes `config.md` as being about the removed flat `.rebar/config.conf` parser; `docs/config.md:13,474` already document it as REMOVED in favor of `rebar.toml` / a `[tool.rebar]` pyproject table.\n- **Stale mypy comment**: `pyproject.toml:457-460` calls non-core type-checking \"advisory-only for now,\" but CI now GATES mypy over the whole library (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:104-108`, \"GATING: mypy over the WHOLE library\").\n\n## Approach\nCorrect each drifted example/label/comment against the CURRENT contract; do not touch behavior. Where a bare handle appears in a quickstart, prefer OMITTING `--assignee` (the `ticket.default_assignee` applies) rather than substituting another example, since the quickstarts already teach claim-without-assignee elsewhere; where an assignee value is genuinely needed for illustration (user-guide.md:229 `edit`), use an email-form (`--assignee=alice@example.com`) that is Jira-resolvable. Fix the two `docs/README.md` navigation/description lines. Rewrite the `pyproject.toml` mypy comment to state the whole tree is gated. This is a docs+comment-only change — no `src/rebar/**` runtime code and no test-behavior changes.\n\n## Scope\n- `README.md` — line 44 assignee example.\n- `docs/user-guide.md` — lines 115 and 229 assignee examples.\n- `docs/README.md` — line 25 (MCP → mcp-reference.md) and line 91 (config.md description → rebar.toml/[tool.rebar]).\n- `pyproject.toml` — the `[tool.mypy]` header comment (457-460) to reflect whole-library gating.\n- (`docs/identity.md:184` legitimately references legacy `.rebar/config.conf` as a per-machine override and is intentionally NOT changed.)\n\n## Verification (docs/comment-only change)\n- No runtime or test behavior changes; the existing docs/link/golden suites (`tests/unit/test_user_guide_dc_docs.py` and the drift gates listed in `docs/README.md:279-293`) stay green.\n- Each corrected truth is confirmed by a grep assertion (below) rather than manual review.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No quickstart teaches a Jira-unresolvable bare handle: `grep -rnE '\\-\\-assignee[= ]+[A-Za-z]+([^@A-Za-z]|$)' README.md docs/user-guide.md` returns NO line whose value lacks an `@` (every remaining `--assignee` example is either omitted or an email-form). \n- [ ] `docs/README.md` line for \"Drive rebar over MCP\" points to `mcp-reference.md` (`grep -n 'Drive rebar over MCP' docs/README.md` line links `mcp-reference.md`, not `llm-framework.md`), and no `docs/README.md` line describes `config.md` via `.rebar/config.conf` (`grep -n 'config\\.conf' docs/README.md` returns nothing).\n- [ ] The `[tool.mypy]` comment no longer calls non-core checking \"advisory-only\": `grep -n 'advisory-only for now' pyproject.toml` returns nothing, and the comment names whole-library gating.\n- [ ] `git diff --name-only` touches only `README.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/README.md`, `pyproject.toml` (no `src/rebar/**`), and the full docs/lint/test suites remain green."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786235299398477001,"uuid":"ed27256a-bbde-485b-9409-e43a2958c6fd"}